Description: Paint the perspective view in stereo with off-axis cameras
 The vertical perspective projection has its camera at a finite distance P: the
 two eyes' cameras are moved sideways by half of the separation (P sin of half
 the angle, seen from the globe's centre), their axes stay parallel and the
 projection is off-axis, with the plane through the globe's centre at zero
 parallax; the stars take the parallax of infinity.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, https://github.com/danielcamposramos (branch stereo3d-perspective, Marble v26.04.0)
Forwarded: no
